                <pb facs="1204" n="1186" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.00/8–1546: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Paraguay</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Beaulac</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-15T12:00:00-04:00">August 15,
                        1946—noon.</date><lb/>[Received 5:54 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>376. Re Embassy telegram 374, August 14, 4 p.m.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d953-f1"/>
                    While press, including Government press, admits students and others interfered
                    with Liberal Party procession Ministry of Interior yesterday issued communiqué
                    placing entire blame on Liberals. Communists, while declaring attitude of
                    students understandable and refraining from attacking Govt, named six
                    individuals most of sinister reputation, as having stirred up students.
                    Communists denied they were involved although it is known they are closely
                    associated with student agitators. One radio station owner arrested and
                    censorship on outgoing press despatches imposed. Govt and parties supporting it
                    have lost prestige because of Government’s evident partiality.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaulac</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d953-f1" n="11" xml:id="d953-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported the reception of the Liberal leader and ex-President
                    José P. Guggiari (834.00/8–1446).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
